{"changes":["(New) Open rekordbox libraries stored on connected drives, choose which drive to use, and reconnect when the drive is missing.","(New) Browse and edit playlists stored on USB devices from the Devices tree.","(New) Find missing tracks in the Missing File Manager, relocate them with search folders, or remove them from the collection.","(New) View and edit metadata for multiple selected tracks at once.","(New) Drop folders onto Playlists to create playlists from their audio files and folder structure.","(New) See Collection tracks that have never been analysed and optionally add a memory cue at each track's first beat during analysis.","(New) Control loops on both decks, resize them live, and start BPM-synced decks on the master's beat.","(New) Show progress while importing a rekordbox or iTunes XML collection.","(Fixed) USB sync now handles interrupted exports, rekordbox background activity, newer device timestamps, disconnected devices, exFAT and older FAT32 sticks, accented filenames, and export failures more reliably.","(Fixed) XML imports ask before replacing same-named playlists, replace their tracks together, and no longer duplicate playlists on repeated imports.","(Fixed) Track previews stop and follow the browser volume correctly when another playlist or deck takes over.","(Fixed) Cloud-synced tracks play from their local Dropbox copy, including on the machine that uploaded them.","(Fixed) Cue and loop editing now follows rekordbox for first-beat cues, quantized hot-cue jumps, short loops, loop-length steps, and memory-cue limits.","(Fixed) Deleting selected tracks acts once, removes every selected track, and asks before removing tracks from playlists, history, or the Tag List.","(Fixed) Long-track waveforms and beat grids now draw through the end of the track.","(Fixed) Backups skip operating-system metadata files and identify the file that prevented a backup from being assembled.","(Fixed) LINK loading now works with XDJ-700 players whose handle